From 75e96f13e1d04e9e6eeea59b325ca2fa4c50ae19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:17:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: name the .aon sources by their extension
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the .aon rename: spec/*.aontu became spec/*.aon, but this
workflow still calls them .aontu in the spec-freshness comments, that job's
display name, the message printed when the artifact is stale, and the
reference to the format shape (spec/def/omni-spec.aon).

Cosmetic only. No CI logic keys off the extension — the job runs `make spec`
and diffs `git status --porcelain -- spec/`, and the shape check globs via
tools/check-spec-shape.js, which the rename already updated — so both have
been passing on the renamed sources throughout; they just report them under
the old name.

Carried as a patch because pushing .github/workflows/ needs a `workflow`
scoped token, which the session that did the rename did not have.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 9071a67..cf4007c 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -254,11 +254,11 @@ jobs:
           echo "$HOME/.elan/bin" >> "$GITHUB_PATH"
       - run: make test-lean
 
-  # spec/*.json is generated from spec/*.aontu and committed so that no port
+  # spec/*.json is generated from spec/*.aon and committed so that no port
   # needs a Node toolchain. Recompile it here and fail if the committed copy
   # differs — a spec edit cannot land with a stale artifact.
   spec-freshness:
-    name: spec regenerates from *.aontu
+    name: spec regenerates from *.aon
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7
@@ -267,19 +267,19 @@ jobs:
           node-version: '24'
       - run: make spec
       # Not `git diff --exit-code`: that ignores untracked files, so a commit
-      # adding a new spec/*.aontu without its generated JSON would pass while
+      # adding a new spec/*.aon without its generated JSON would pass while
       # the artifact the ports read was never committed at all.
       - name: Fail if a committed spec JSON is stale or missing
         run: |
           if [ -n "$(git status --porcelain -- spec/)" ]; then
             git status --porcelain -- spec/
             echo
-            echo "spec/ is out of sync with its .aontu sources."
+            echo "spec/ is out of sync with its .aon sources."
             echo "Run 'make spec' and commit the result."
             exit 1
           fi
       # A well-formed spec, not just a fresh artifact: unify each spec
-      # source with the format shape (spec/def/omni-spec.aontu), which is
+      # source with the format shape (spec/def/omni-spec.aon), which is
       # itself aontu. --self-test proves the shape can still go red.
       - name: Check spec sources against the format shape
         run: cd tools && npm run --silent check-spec-shape
-- 
